  "summary": "DIR-060 PHASE 2 COMPLETE (permanent fix) under the OPTION A ruling; templates remain AUDIT-ONLY and UNTOUCHED. IDENTIFY->PROVE: ResumeWatermarkOverlay decided purely on the global admin setting (watermark.enableFreeWatermark) with NO entitlement input; the render sites read values._watermark || values.watermark (TemplateRenderer.jsx:58, SmartResumeComposer.jsx:76) but _watermark is written NOWHERE in src/, and the builder preview view model (BuildResume.jsx:959) carried neither a watermark nor an entitlement, while removesWatermark existed ONLY in backend/. Consequence: FREE users got NO watermark in preview, and any caller supplying the global watermark would stamp a PAID document. RCA->FIX (non-frozen, permanent): new src/utils/watermarkEntitlement.js with a fail-closed shouldRenderWatermark() + resolvePreviewWatermark() + readEntitlement(); ResumeWatermarkOverlay now delegates to it and accepts an explicit entitlement; BOTH render sites pass entitlement={readEntitlement(values)}; BuildResume previewData now publishes _watermark (from public_config.watermark gated by isPaidMembershipTier) and _entitlement. FROZEN BOUNDARY RESPECTED: git status shows NO file under src/cv-templates/ modified - all 51 resume + 4 cover dirs untouched (asserted). EVIDENCE: new suite 9/9; template/export regression 70/70 (incl. server-rendering every template); full product matrix 756 pass/0 fail; eslint 0 errors; build exit 0 in 3.58s. HONEST LIMITS: the per-template A4/overflow audit matrix, the HeadingStep hydration audit and the PDF<->DOCX parity run are NOT yet done - head-start measurements recorded in the evidence doc (.bridge/evidence/dir060-implementation-evidence.md)."
